<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buluggin ibn Ziri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 984</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Bulukkin ibn Ziri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buluggin ibn Ziri was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanhaja">Sanhaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> leader, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziri-ibn-manad">Ziri ibn Manad</a>, and the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zirid-dynasty">Zirid dynasty</a>. When the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mu'izz moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 972, he made Buluggin governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>, Buluggin campaigned across the central and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> against the Zenata and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buluggin-ibn-ziri.jpg" alt="Buluggin ibn Ziri" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_de_Bologhine_ibn_Ziri_(Alger).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
